slides.code:
.box {
  background: blue;
}

/* screen 768px or smaller */
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .box {
    background: red;
  }
}

/* mobile-first: phone first */
.box { font-size: 16px; }

/* from 768px up we add */
@media (min-width: 768px) {
  .box { font-size: 24px; }
}

.menu {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: row;       /* desktop */
  gap: 20px;
}
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .menu {
    flex-direction: column;  /* phone */
  }
}

.gallery {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);  /* desktop */
  gap: 20px;
}
@media (max-width: 1024px) {
  .gallery { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }  /* tablet */
}
@media (max-width: 600px) {
  .gallery { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }  /* phone */
}

slides.text:
Adapt everything you made over 3 weeks (cards, menu, landing) to 3 screens. Check yourself:
— every HTML has meta viewport;
— two breakpoints: `max-width: 1024px` and `max-width: 600px`;
— no horizontal scroll on a phone and nothing is cut off;
— 3 screenshots: phone, tablet, computer (in DevTools).
